# Burn Engine servings & food-list gram weights

This system is **not** straight calorie/macro counting. The Burn Engine builds a plan once; the user follows **servings** and weighs food to **gram portions** on the approved list. Agents must keep food-list weights, prep labels, PDF printouts, and `data/foods.json` aligned with these rules.

## Core principle

**A serving is defined by grams of the target macro, with a fat ceiling in grams — not by calories.**

| Wrong | Right |
|-------|-------|
| “32 calories of protein per serving” | **8g protein** per serving, **≤2g fat** |
| “56 calories of carbs per grain serving” | **14g carbs** per serving |
| “40 calories of vegetables” | **10g carbs** per serving |
| Weigh food without knowing prep state | Gram weight only valid for the **labeled prep** (dry / cooked / raw) |

The engine’s internal loops use calorie weights (32, 56, 40, 72…) to balance the plan in `js/burnEngine.js`. **User-facing portions and food-list gram weights use macro grams + fat limits.**

## Daily servings (what the user follows)

From `computeServingsPhase` in `js/burnEngine.js`:

| User-facing group | Engine slots | Notes |
|-------------------|--------------|-------|
| **Protein** | `P1` + `D1` | One number on Servings page; includes dairy |
| **Grains & starches** | `G1` + `S2` | One number on Servings page |
| **Vegetables** | `VE` | Always **1** daily |
| **Fruits** | `FQ` | Minimum **3** daily |
| **Extra fat** | `FT` | `fatMaintain` / `fatReduce` on Servings page |

`P1` = non-dairy protein (meat, fish, egg whites). `D1` = dairy. `G1` = grains. `S2` = starches. Engine keeps grains vs starches separate for **fat limits** even though the user sees one combined count.

## One serving — macro targets (make the cut)

Use these when sizing **base** `gramWeight` in `data/foods.json`, `CUTTING_STAPLES_*` rows, and audits. These are **one-serving** reference weights before any PDF scaling.

### Non-dairy protein (`P1`)

| Macro | Per serving |
|-------|-------------|
| Protein | **8g** |
| Fat | **≤2g** |

Gram weight ≈ `800 / protein_per_100g`, then verify fat ≤ 2g at that weight. **1982 seminar tested weights override USDA** where they differ (`scripts/protein-82-audit.mjs`, `docs/knowledge-base-backlog.md`).

### Dairy (`D1`)

Counts toward **protein** servings on the Servings page. Engine also assigns **12g carbs** and ~2.4g fat per dairy serving in internal loops. Portion weights on the food list are **curated per item** (milk, yogurt, cottage cheese) — do not assume the same gram formula as meat/fish.

### Grains (`G1`)

| Macro | Per serving |
|-------|-------------|
| Carbs | **14g** |
| Fat | **≤1.0g** (“14/1”) |

Gram weight ≈ `1400 / carbs_per_100g`. **Dry** for oats, grits, farina, cream of wheat — user adds water (`servingDescription: "dry"`). **Cooked** for rice, pasta, quinoa. Audit: `scripts/grains-14-1-audit.mjs`.

### Starches (`S2`)

| Macro | Per serving |
|-------|-------------|
| Carbs | **14g** |
| Fat | **≤0.44g** (“14/0.44”) |

Same carb target as grains; **stricter fat cap**. Beans, potatoes, corn, peas, squash. Audit: `scripts/starches-14-0-audit.mjs`.

### Vegetables (`VE`)

| Macro | Per serving |
|-------|-------------|
| Carbs | **10g** |
| Fat | **≤3g** |

Gram weight ≈ `1000 / carbs_per_100g`. **Raw and cooked are separate catalog entries** when both exist — different gram weights. Audit: `scripts/veg-fruit-audit.mjs`.

### Fruits (`FQ`)

Engine fruit slot uses **72 calories** per serving in balancing loops (differs from carb-gram categories above). Food-list audit: **≤4g fat** at the portion; gram weight from calorie density (`7200 / kcal_per_100g` in comments). User still follows **servings**, not calories.

### Extra fat (`FT`)

**45 calories** per point (`FAT_SERVING_CALORIES` in `js/burnEngine.js`). Separate from food-list staple rows.

## Why prep state matters

Gram weight only works if the user knows **how that food is measured**:

| Prep | Examples | Rule |
|------|----------|------|
| **dry** | Oatmeal, grits, farina | Weigh **dry**; user adds water |
| **cooked** | Rice, pasta, mushrooms, broccoli | Weigh **after cooking** — what goes on the plate |
| **raw** | Cucumber, some salads | Eaten as-is |

Cooking changes water content → **carbs/protein per 100g change** → **different gram weights** for the same macro serving. Raw vs cooked gaps can be large (e.g. mushrooms). **Never interchange raw and cooked gram weights.**

Tips source: `data/*TipsPrintout.js` — “Measure serving sizes after cooking” where applicable.

