## PDF & printout system (three layers)

The user does **not** do serving × gram math themselves. Three surfaces split the job:

| Layer | What it shows | Example (chicken, 3 protein servings at lunch) |
|-------|---------------|--------------------------------------------------|
| **1 — Servings page** | Serving **counts** only (`3`, `4.3`, `9`…) | `3` at lunch — **no grams** |
| **2 — Food list (program report PDF)** | **Math done** — plan slot servings × one-serving gram weight | `78g` (3 × 26g) |
| **3 — Meal plan / grocery list (Print Shop)** | **Math done** — assigned servings × gram weight | `78g` for that meal slot |

**Layer 1** = counts to follow. **Layers 2 & 3** = gram totals so the user weighs food, not multiplies.

### KWarner program report PDF (locked preview)

Work in the **KWarner locked preview pipeline** for program-report printout changes — see `.cursor/rules/kwarner-preview-pdf.mdc`.

| Page | Content | Grams? |
|------|---------|--------|
| Welcome | Intro copy | No |
| Projections | LBM, timeline | No |
| Food Plan | Macro signal, inputs | No |
| **Servings** | Daily + meal/snack grid (`servingsGridRows`) | **Counts only** |
| **Food list** | Protein, grains, vegetables, fruit staples | **Scaled grams** |
| Flavor kits | Shop checklist (no gram servings) | No |

Renderer: `server/pdf/renderProgramReportKwarnerLockedPreview.js`.  
Payload: `js/programReportPrintout.js` → `payload.servings.planServings` + `payload.servings.gridRows`.

### Food list scaling (layer 2)

At PDF render time, staple rows are scaled from the user’s plan via `js/stapleServingPrintout.js`:

```
displayed grams = plan slot servings × one-serving gram weight
```

| Food-list section | Multiplier (`stapleCategoryServings`) |
|-------------------|---------------------------------------|
| Protein + dairy | `planServings.protein / 3` (per meal) |
| Grains & starches | `planServings.grainsStarches / 3` (per meal) |
| Vegetables | `planServings.vegetables` (daily) |
| Fruit | `planServings.fruits / 3` (per snack) |

- **Base** one-serving weights: `data/cuttingStaplesPrintout.js` (`CUTTING_STAPLES_*`) and `catalogStapleRow()` from `data/foods.json`.
- **Scaled** labels: `scaleStapleRows()` → `drawStapleListRow()` in the KWarner renderer.
- Count-based labels (e.g. `2 whites`) scale the same way: 3 protein servings → `6 whites`.

Kristi example: 9 protein daily → 3 per meal → chicken `26g` base → **`78g`** on food list PDF.

### Print Shop — meal plan & grocery (layer 3)

From menu planner when the user has assigned foods:

| Document | Path | Scaling |
|----------|------|---------|
| Weekly meal plan | `server/pdf/renderWeekPlan.js` | `gramWeightLabel()` via `plannerPrintPayload.js` |
| Grocery list | `server/pdf/renderShoppingList.js` | `foodAmountLabel()` — weekly totals |

Client: `menuplanner/js/plannerPrintPayload.js` → `printFoodAmount()` → `gramWeightLabel()` in `plannerState.js`.

Generic Print Shop food list (`renderFoodList.js`, view `foodlist`) is a **separate** static catalog (names + tips, no personalized grams). Personalized gram math lives on the **program report food-list pages** and **menu planner** printouts above.

