## Agent checklist

Before changing food-list gram weights, PDF staple columns, or `foods.json`:

1. Identify **category** (P1, D1, G1, S2, VE, FQ) and use the **macro-gram target**, not calories.
2. Confirm **prep state** (dry / cooked / raw) matches how the user measures that line item.
3. Verify **fat at portion** against the category limit — that sets the **base** one-serving `gramWeight`.
4. **Servings PDF** = counts only; **program report food list** = `stapleCategoryServings` × base weight; **meal plan / grocery** = assigned servings × `gramWeight`.
5. Run relevant audit script; for KWarner PDF changes also `npm run render:kwarner-preview` and push per `.cursor/rules/kwarner-preview-pdf.mdc`.
